.TH OPENDIALD 1 "2026-11-10" "OpenDial 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
opendiald \- Surface Dial service: radial menu, tools, profiles and haptics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opendiald
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B opendiald
runs in the user session, reads the Microsoft Surface Dial through evdev,
drives its haptics through hidraw, shows the radial menu and performs the
actions of the active tool. It is normally started by the systemd user unit
.B opendial.service
or by D-Bus activation and is configured with
.BR opendial (1)
or
.BR opendialctl (1).
Only one instance runs per session (D-Bus name \fBio.github.opendial\fR).
.PP
It never runs as root. Device access is granted to the active seat user by the
udev rule \fB70-opendial-surface-dial.rules\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-device
Do not open the Surface Dial; input only comes from simulation.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-context
Do not track the focused window (app profiles only change when locked).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Log actions instead of sending keys, scrolling, volume changes or running
programs. Tool, profile and menu logic still run.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-overlay
Do not show the radial menu or on-screen feedback.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tray
Do not show a tray icon.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Use \fIpath\fR instead of \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/opendial/config.json\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-state " path"
Use \fIpath\fR instead of \fI$XDG_STATE_HOME/opendial/state.json\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-replay " file"
Feed a recorded fixture (JSON lines or evtest text) through the decoder and engine.
.TP
.BI \-\-replay\-speed " x"
Replay speed factor (gesture timing is wall clock: use 1 for long presses).
.TP
.B \-\-exit\-after\-replay
Print the event log as JSON lines and exit when the replay finished.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Debug logging.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/opendial/config.json
Tools, profiles and settings (validated, written atomically, five backups).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/opendial/state.json
Active tool per profile, locked profile, approvals, plugin consent.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-opendial-surface-dial.rules
Device access for the active seat user.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on normal exit (also when another instance already runs), 1 on startup
failure, 2 for an unreadable replay fixture.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR opendial (1),
.BR opendialctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
